From 1ef4baf678a3f213338f8495b3c7a744f3671486 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CNY Healthcare <cnyhealthymall@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 16:45:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] fix(send): quiet hours refuse a send_now instead of
 warning after the fact
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`quietHoursCheck()` produced a warning that was appended to the `warnings[]`
of a `success: true` reply — which means the message had already gone out by
the time anyone could read it. A human might feel bad about it; an autonomous
agent has no reason to act on a warning attached to a success, so nothing
stopped a promo from shipping at 02:00. `force: true` therefore did not
"override" a block, it only suppressed the text.

mode='send_now' now refuses inside 22:00-08:00 BKK and says how to proceed
(`force=true`, or mode='draft' to schedule in OA Manager). dry_run and draft
are untouched — neither delivers anything, so both still just warn.

The verdict and the message now share one pinned `now`, so a send landing
exactly on 22:00:00 cannot report a different hour than the one it refused on.

Note for CI: this makes any unpinned send_now test time-dependent — it would
pass by day and fail nightly. The two suites that exercise send_now through
the MCP surface now pin a daytime clock in beforeEach (Date only, real
timers), which the happy-path test was already doing locally for exactly this
reason.

Tests: the previously pinned "warning-only" behaviour is replaced by its
opposite — blocked with zero /push and zero /quota traffic — plus force=true
sending clean, dry_run and draft staying unblocked, and a 21:59:59 / 22:00:00
boundary pair driven through the tool.
